WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.810 --> 00:00:03.000
The Little Red Hen

2
00:00:06.750 --> 00:00:10.540
(A version of the tale by TheFableCottage.com)

3
00:00:14.850 --> 00:00:19.190
This is a story about a little red hen.

4
00:00:19.970 --> 00:00:23.580
The little red hen lives on a farm.

5
00:00:23.730 --> 00:00:27.180
She works hard all day long:

6
00:00:27.330 --> 00:00:29.650
She pecks the ground.

7
00:00:30.000 --> 00:00:32.250
She looks for worms.

8
00:00:32.630 --> 00:00:35.330
She sits in a bush.

9
00:00:35.690 --> 00:00:39.310
And sometimes… she lays an egg.

10
00:00:41.100 --> 00:00:44.190
The little red hen has three friends:

11
00:00:44.340 --> 00:00:45.440
A cat

12
00:00:45.570 --> 00:00:46.540
A dog

13
00:00:46.540 --> 00:00:47.760
And a horse.

14
00:00:48.780 --> 00:00:52.180
These animals don’t work hard at all.

15
00:00:52.940 --> 00:00:55.670
The cat likes to sleep in the sun.

16
00:00:56.240 --> 00:00:59.060
The dog likes to sleep in the shade.

17
00:00:59.550 --> 00:01:05.490
And the horse likes to  watch TV all day long.

18
00:01:06.210 --> 00:01:11.000
One day the little red hen  sees a raspberry bush.

19
00:01:12.110 --> 00:01:15.190
Raspberries!” she squeals.

20
00:01:15.320 --> 00:01:20.570
“Yum yum yum!  We can make a raspberry cake!”

21
00:01:21.570 --> 00:01:25.690
The little red hen runs to tell her friends.

22
00:01:25.880 --> 00:01:29.570
“Guys! There are raspberries over there!

23
00:01:29.680 --> 00:01:32.660
We can make a raspberry cake!”

24
00:01:33.710 --> 00:01:37.740
The dog drools. "Yes!"

25
00:01:38.000 --> 00:01:44.890
The cat licks her lips. "Absolutely!"

26
00:01:45.000 --> 00:01:51.380
The horse flicks his tail. "What a great idea!"

27
00:01:52.550 --> 00:01:59.510
So… who wants to help me pick the raspberries?”  asks the little red hen.

28
00:01:59.910 --> 00:02:04.580
“Not me,” says the dog, “I’m too busy.”

29
00:02:05.020 --> 00:02:11.190
“Not me,” says the cat,  “I’m too tired.”

30
00:02:11.620 --> 00:02:16.780
“Not me,” says the horse,  “I’m watching TV.”

31
00:02:18.800 --> 00:02:23.640
"Then I will do it myself,”  says the little red hen.

32
00:02:23.650 --> 00:02:29.840
So she picks the berries, one by one,  all by herself.

33
00:02:36.630 --> 00:02:45.480
"Ok, now we need flour, and sugar, and milk, and butter," says the little red hen.

34
00:02:45.830 --> 00:02:48.400
“Who wants to help me get them?”

35
00:02:48.750 --> 00:02:54.290
“Not me,” says the dog,  “I’m too busy.”

36
00:02:55.350 --> 00:03:00.930
“Not me,” says the cat,  “I’m too tired.”

37
00:03:01.780 --> 00:03:07.960
“Not me,” says the horse,  “I’m watching TV.”

38
00:03:10.970 --> 00:03:16.140
“Then I will do it myself,”  says the little red hen.

39
00:03:16.330 --> 00:03:23.420
She goes all the way to the pantry  and gets the flour and the sugar.

40
00:03:23.530 --> 00:03:30.080
She goes all the way to the fridge  and gets the butter and the milk.

41
00:03:30.510 --> 00:03:37.240
Then she puts everything together into a big bowl,  all by herself.

42
00:03:40.960 --> 00:03:46.560
“Who wants to help me mix the cake batter?”  asks the little red hen.

43
00:03:46.620 --> 00:03:52.930
“Not me,” says the dog,  “I’m too busy.”

44
00:03:53.850 --> 00:04:00.220
“Not me,” says the cat,  “I’m too tired.”

45
00:04:01.310 --> 00:04:07.460
“Not me,” says the horse,  “I’m watching TV.”

46
00:04:08.010 --> 00:04:14.410
“Then I will do it myself!”  says the little red hen.

47
00:04:14.890 --> 00:04:19.400
She mixes the batter until it is  smooth and creamy.

48
00:04:19.860 --> 00:04:23.890
Then she gently stirs through the raspberries.

49
00:04:24.620 --> 00:04:27.920
She pours the batter into a cake tin.

50
00:04:28.090 --> 00:04:33.000
Then she puts it in the oven.  All by herself.

51
00:04:33.710 --> 00:04:36.580
(Tick tock, tick tock)

52
00:04:37.230 --> 00:04:42.060
Soon there is a delicious smell  coming from the kitchen.

53
00:04:42.450 --> 00:04:44.450
The dog can smell it.

54
00:04:45.210 --> 00:04:47.210
The cat can smell it.

55
00:04:48.000 --> 00:04:50.600
The horse can smell it too.

56
00:04:51.090 --> 00:04:54.090
They all rush to the kitchen.

57
00:04:55.160 --> 00:04:58.960
The little red hen takes the cake from the oven.

58
00:04:59.120 --> 00:05:03.220
She puts it on a plate and sprinkles it with sugar.

59
00:05:04.470 --> 00:05:11.640
“So… Who wants to help me eat this cake?”  asks the little red hen.

60
00:05:11.880 --> 00:05:15.510
“Me!” Says the dog.

61
00:05:15.610 --> 00:05:18.970
“Me!”  Says the cat.

62
00:05:19.220 --> 00:05:22.340
“Me!” Says the horse.

63
00:05:23.170 --> 00:05:28.340
“I don’t think so,” says the little red hen.

64
00:05:28.520 --> 00:05:35.020
“You would not help me make this cake…   so you will not help me eat it.”

65
00:05:35.110 --> 00:05:41.250
She runs away with the cake  and eats every last crumb.

66
00:05:41.410 --> 00:05:44.540
All by herself.
